# Secrets never enter the build context. The build stage does `COPY . .`, so an operator's local
# `.env` landed in an image layer — one that `cache-to=type=gha,mode=max` then pushes to a shared
# cache. `.env.example` is the committed template and is the one file here that must survive.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
# Same shape, different file: an `.npmrc` carries a registry auth token, none is tracked in this
# repo, so any that exists is somebody's local credential and has no business in a layer.
**/.npmrc

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.x
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
docs
site
wiki
coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
